hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15801","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, from al-Qasim, from Salih ibn Khawwat, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah: as for Abd al-Rahman, he raised it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and as for Yahya, he mentioned from Sahl, he said: The imam stands with a row behind him and a row in front of him, and he prays with those behind him one rakah and two prostrations, then he stands upright until they pray another rakah, then they advance to the place of their companions, then those come and stand in the place of these, and he prays with them one rakah and two prostrations, then he sits until they complete another rakah, then he greets them."
"15802","Rawh narrated to us: Shubah and Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Salih ibn Khawwat, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: He prays with those behind him one rakah and two prostrations, then he sits in his place until they complete one rakah and two prostrations, then they move to the station of their companions, then their companions move to the place of these, and he mentioned its meaning."
"15803","Rawh narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Salih ibn Khawwat, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of this."
"15804","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari informed me, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Masud ibn Niyar say: Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah came to our gathering and narrated that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you estimate the fruit, then harvest and leave; leave a third, and if you do not harvest and leave, then leave a fourth."
